              <p class="text-gray-700">It depends on the product and climate. Premium polymer sealers like BLACK JACK Drive-Maxx 1000 are rated up to 10 years, thicker acrylics like Latex-ite Airport Grade last 3–5 years, and budget sealers usually need recoating every 2–3 years. Concrete penetrating sealers like Foundation Armor SX5000 can last 7–10 years, while film-forming wet-look sealers last 2–5 years. Surface prep and proper application weather matter as much as the product.</p>
